## Proposed seal contract

1. Select original AST nodes from the maintained rolldown parser. Require
   exactly one matching runtime declaration for each approved name. Refuse
   missing, duplicate, destructured, or otherwise unsupported selections.
   The invocation helper declaration(text, name) is not the seal extractor:
   it first-matches and reconstructs variable declarators as const.
2. Preserve the original VariableDeclaration kind and its selected original
   declarator. Never normalize let or var to const. Preserve class heritage,
   fields, initializers, constructors, private methods, getters, setters,
   computed keys, static blocks, decorators, and member order when selecting
   a whole named class. Apply the existing metadata cleaning and SHA-256
   procedure to these original nodes.
3. Add a module-shell record for each of the five owners. It covers every
   runtime import binding and source, side-effect import, runtime export and
   re-export, default-export expression, and top-level non-declaration
   executable statement. It also covers every top-level runtime variable
   initializer and its declaration kind. Module execution order is retained.
   An unsupported executable construct fails closed instead of disappearing.
   Named declaration exports contribute their name, kind, modifiers, and
   export shape to the shell, not a second copy of their bodies. Anonymous
   default-export expressions remain full executable AST. Keep the module
   prelude and ordered declaration-name inventory, so a new owner, changed
   import, or added initializer cannot fall between selected declarations.
4. Record the declaration-name/kind inventory in the shell. A new, removed,
   or changed-kind runtime declaration requires a reviewed coverage decision.
   For an explicitly unselected function, record its identity but exclude
   its body. No unselected executable initializer is permitted. Type-only
   interfaces, aliases, and imports are outside this runtime-shell proposal;
   normal type checking remains required.
5. Give each selected declaration its own explicit seal record. Hashing a
   file name plus a list into one large fingerprint would preserve the same
   hot-line conflict and is not the intended table shape. A failure emits
   one finite line naming file, declaration, actual maintained-parser hash,
   and the rule requiring source review before adoption. Do not emit source.

This contract preserves import rewiring and module-initializer coverage
which function-body hashes alone would lose. It is a tripwire design, not
proof that an imported implementation or injected port grants authority.

