## Why these roots and helpers stay

- ScopeObject retains construction/wiring and every native ingress wrapper.
  Its context, invocation, read preparation, creation-pin, session, proof,
  archive, and alarm paths share private state. observed uses computed
  this[method] dispatch. The imported OBSERVED_METHODS binding and every
  dispatchable method must remain covered. Selecting only submit would miss
  that wiring and the signed prepare/read paths.
- Scope retains create, submit, prepare, standing, settle, floor, alarm,
  checkpoint, and their common state. Same-module helpers include Received,
  Observes, receiptOf, ownOf, snapshotsOf, used, retainedFacts, creationKind,
  besideOf, valuesBeside, valuesOf, NO_INCARNATION, unavailable, said, heldBy,
  and told. The conservative set also protects exported helpers even where
  a direct-this walk does not establish their external callers.
- Worker coverage keeps api, route/routedRequest, mcpRoute, outsideOf,
  sessionWiring, snapshotReaderOf, and every exported Durable Object or
  WorkerEntrypoint class, including the currently unbound ScopeService.
  Its response/body/status helpers, size constants, boundedBytes,
  observeThrough, sqlOf, and ApplicationStreamLifetime stay named and
  protected. The inventory still executes its existing matcher model with
  stand-ins. No matcher, route, gate class, or model changes here.
- McpService retains constructor dispatch composition, fresh snapshot and
  admission, generic tool admission, target checks, perform, create/install,
  settlement, credential, and the methods they reach. Its same-module
  argument parsers, output/privacy bounds, READ/WRITE sets, error handling,
  and generation helpers stay covered. genericTools mixes prose with
  dispatch/schema composition; description edits there still require a seal
  update. No claim is made that declaration selection removes that coupling.
- CLI coverage retains install selection and retained-plan custody, join,
  invitation, act, mutation, and credential/clone paths. All their current
  same-module helpers remain in the explicit set. Read and replay entry
  declarations remain protected conservatively; this head does not silently
  drop them through an incomplete mutating-call graph.

## Demonstrated unrelated declaration

Only packages/cli/src/commands.ts:entryLine is proposed as an unselected
body. At this exact head its only callers are log and show. The function
formats an already returned entry for display. It performs no request,
key lookup, signing, storage, grant check, or token handoff. Keep its binding
identity in the module shell so deleting it, changing its kind, or replacing
it with a module-executed initializer cannot pass unnoticed. An edit only
to its display wording is the concrete negative control: named gate seals
and the unchanged route inventory should remain equal. This does not exempt
log or show themselves. No other unselected runtime body is claimed safe.

Type-only top-level declarations are also outside runtime declaration
coverage. A type change can still fail TypeScript; its omission from a
security seal does not make it a runtime acceptance claim.

